Z||000000||mrfiero||04-22-2001||10:00 PM||||My 16K mile '88 GT needs new tires.......mine are half worn and hard as a rock (I can peel out for half a block, and it's an auto!).  I might have a line on a set of 215/60-15 GT+4's, but that still leaves the fronts (205/60-15).<P>Does anyone have any ideas?<P>I will check with Goodyear in the morning, but figured I'd ask here first.  <P>BTW......I am not interested in any other tires except the original GT+4's.  I want to keep it as original as possible.<p>[This message has been edited by mrfiero (edited 04-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||fiero56||04-22-2001||10:17 PM||||Mike, would any unused GT+4 be NOS? I looked into getting a set for my Formula 1.5 years ago, but ended up going with a different brand. One of the local shops here could get me a set, correct sizes, I think price was like $350 for a set. If you want, I can check and see if they can get their hands on a set, but shipping to CO might be killer, I don't know.||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfiero||04-22-2001||10:22 PM||||NOS means new old stock, so yes......if a tire has not been mounted it would be considered NOS.  <P>Find out if they can get them at that price.  I will actually be in the area next week.....I'll be driving up to Michigan to pick up a set of leather seats, so picking up some tires in Ohio wouldn't be a big stretch.  <P>LMK.  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||fiero56||04-22-2001||10:26 PM||||I'll ceck with them tommorrow. I wasn't sure what NOS meant to you. Didn't know if you were just looking for any unused set, or for a "new" set previously mounted on a Fiero(I know of several people <B>that</B>anal <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">).||||reg||1
Z||000004||Rodney||04-23-2001||09:32 AM||||Goodyear has a department that keeps track of NOS tires. 1-800-321-2136. If you don't get a good person call back and hopefully try a different one. ||||reg||1
